error[NK1125]: A `String?` may be missing, so you can't reach its method directly.
  --> tests/a_different_literal_is_not_the_same_part.nika:4:5
   |
 4 |     return match (n, why) { (1, null) => 0, (2, w) => w.len(), (_, _) => -1 }
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A `T?` is its own type, not a `T` that might be missing, so it doesn't have `T`'s members. That's why a missing value can never crash here.
   = help: Write `?.len(…)`, which gives `null` when the value is missing, or give a fallback with `??` first and reach into that.
